{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2443","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2443","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2443\",\"parent_revision\":\"b0678754eb9cf45bbd59867d89c78a38ef2972b51861cffa0563d54db5243b27\",\"root_revision\":\"b0678754eb9cf45bbd59867d89c78a38ef2972b51861cffa0563d54db5243b27\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThree acceptance criteria check_commands in plan Pdec8934d have design gaps that cause them to report still_failing even when the implementation is correct:\\n\\nAC4/AC5: Use BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads to test SAM task routing. The correct variable is TASKBACKEND=beads. BACKLOG_BACKEND routes backlog operations, TASKBACKEND routes SAM task operations (BeadsTaskProvider). AC4/AC5 will always report failure regardless of BeadsTaskProvider implementation because they set the wrong env var.\\n\\nAC6: Tests that int(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\") raises ValueError. This is always true regardless of any code change and proves nothing about the task_status_hook beads ID handling. The test was intended to verify the hook no longer casts parent_issue_number to int, but the check_command tests the wrong behavior.\\n\\nIf a TN verification run is triggered on Pdec8934d, these three criteria will report regressions and block completion even though the implementation is correct. The check_commands must be amended before the next TN run.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **pdec8934d tn check_commands ac4/ac5/ac6 have design gaps \u2014 test wrong env vars and behavior** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: QG T6 context refinement note, session 2026-05-15\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Completeness Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nAll required inputs are AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE from primary sources.\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description: amend AC4/AC5/AC6 check_commands in Pdec8934d |\\n| Scope boundary | AVAILABLE | Three specific ACs in one plan \u2014 nothing else |\\n| Environment variable semantics | AVAILABLE | `backend_protocol.py` line 935/1046: `BACKLOG_BACKEND` controls backlog provider; `backend-providers.md` line 92/207: `TASKBACKEND` controls SAM task backend |\\n| AC6 failure mode | AVAILABLE | Description: `int(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` is a tautology \u2014 always raises ValueError regardless of hook state |\\n| Correct behavior to test | DERIVABLE | From `task_status_hook.py`: `parent_issue_number` typed `str | int | None` at lines 375, 771, 851 \u2014 the fix was to accept string nanoids without casting |\\n| Verification method | AVAILABLE | Run the corrected check_commands against the plan |\\n\\n**Missing inputs**: None blocking planning or execution.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks**: Any future TN verification run on plan Pdec8934d \u2014 AC4, AC5, and AC6 will report still_failing even when the implementation is correct, blocking plan completion\\n- **False negatives on AC4/AC5**: `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` sets the backlog provider, not the SAM task backend. BeadsTaskProvider is never activated \u2014 the check tests nothing about SAM routing.\\n- **AC6 false negative**: `int(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` raises ValueError unconditionally \u2014 the assertion cannot distinguish between pre-fix and post-fix hook behaviour.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAC4 and AC5 check_commands set `TASKBACKEND=beads` (not `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads`) to route SAM task operations through BeadsTaskProvider. `BACKLOG_BACKEND` controls the backlog provider \u2014 it has no effect on SAM task routing.\\n\\nAC6 check_command exercises the hook with a beads nanoid string as `parent_issue_number` input and asserts it does not raise TypeError and does not attempt int() conversion \u2014 observable from hook exit code or output, not from a standalone int() call.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nPlan Pdec8934d's check_commands for AC4, AC5, and AC6 are amended so that:\\n\\n- AC4/AC5 use `TASKBACKEND=beads` to activate BeadsTaskProvider for SAM operations\\n- AC6 exercises the hook itself with a beads nanoid as `parent_issue_number` input and asserts no TypeError is raised and no int() cast is attempted\\n- All three check_commands produce a meaningful pass/fail signal that changes depending on whether the implementation under test is correct\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. No check_command in AC4 or AC5 of Pdec8934d contains `BACKLOG_BACKEND` \u2014 verified by reading the plan YAML\\n2. Both AC4 and AC5 check_commands contain `TASKBACKEND=beads` \u2014 verified by reading the plan YAML\\n3. AC6 check_command does not contain a standalone `int(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` call or any tautological expression that is always true regardless of hook state\\n4. AC6 check_command exercises the actual hook code path with a beads-format `parent_issue_number` value (e.g. `bd-a3f8`) and the assertion outcome differs between pre-fix and post-fix hook state\\n5. Running the amended TN verification against Pdec8934d produces PASS for AC4, AC5, and AC6 when the underlying implementation is correct\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Source: BACKLOG_BACKEND semantics | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` lines 933-1046 |\\n| Source: TASKBACKEND semantics | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` lines 92, 205-215 |\\n| Source: parent_issue_number typing | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` lines 375, 771, 851 |\\n| Skill | /dh:start-task (plan address syntax reference) |\\n| Related issue | #2441 (duplicate \u2014 Chore variant of this same item, closed as duplicate) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: Plan Pdec8934d being accessible in the active session (locate plan file via SAM backend or filesystem)\\n- Blocks: Future TN verification runs on Pdec8934d \u2014 currently blocked by false-negative check_commands\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 three targeted check_command string replacements in a single plan YAML file. No code changes required. The correct env var (`TASKBACKEND`) and correct AC6 behaviour (no `int()` cast of nanoid) are both confirmed from primary sources.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: Bug (defect in test design \u2014 check_commands assert the wrong conditions)\\n\\n**Root cause category**: Defect \u2014 incorrect environment variable name used in AC4/AC5 check_commands; tautological assertion in AC6 check_command.\\n\\n**Origin**: QG T6 context refinement note, session 2026-05-15. Identified during P60d669b9/T2 feature verification (issue #2279).\\n\",\"digest\":\"c816560bb68f423d2b579612427d5b18434063321605f5a783df3c675d88bdf6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCOWGA\"}"}